1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
94.8% of the top million websites fail accessibility.
This clinic page is one of them.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:15,000
To a blind patient, this photo is "IMG_2041.jpg" and every form field
is just "edit text". They can't book a doctor.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Checkers list problems. Overlays hide them. Nobody fixes the code.
So we built PasteProof.

4
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Ctrl+V. That's the whole workflow.
52 accessibility failures — gone in under two seconds.

5
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:40,000
49 fixes to the actual source code —
and every single one re-audited and verified.

6
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:52,000
The photo gets alt text from Florence-2, a vision model running
inside your browser. No upload. No API key. Free.

7
00:00:52,000 --> 00:01:02,000
It connects the labels already on screen, makes mouse-only buttons
work with a keyboard, and marks required fields.

8
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:12,000
You stay in control: edit any guess, reject any fix, re-run —
and it's verified again.

9
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:27,000
This is what a screen reader says. Before: 12 controls and images with no name.
After: zero. Every field, every link, every image speaks.

10
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:37,000
And the page looks exactly the same. We measure it:
every element keeps its position and size.

11
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:44,000
You get a clean diff of real HTML and CSS — not a runtime script.

12
00:01:44,000 --> 00:02:02,000
Real websites too. Hacker News: 280 failures. PasteProof follows the colors
into the external stylesheet and fixes 241 low-contrast texts
with just six CSS rules — plus a patch for news.css.

13
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:16,000
Pages behind a login — benefit portals, school accounts — one click on the
bookmarklet sends the live page to PasteProof. Nothing leaves your machine.

14
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:26,000
For developers, the same engine runs in CI:
it blocks any deploy that ships new barriers.

15
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:44,000
We tested it on 21 pages, including IRS, NYC.gov, HealthCare.gov and 211.
1,604 issues down to 15. 781 of 781 fixes verified.
Zero new problems. 100% of text and layout preserved.

16
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:50,000
On W3C's own broken demo site, we leave fewer issues than
W3C's expert hand-fixed version: 18 versus 79.

17
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:55,000
PasteProof. Ctrl+V — and the web opens up for everyone.
